  "title": "Chocolate sauce",
  "description": "Your sauce will taste even better if you will use heavy cream. Unfortunatly most of the time I use milk, since I'm always trying to lose weight 😉 but it keeps finding me for some reason.",
  "editorial": {
    "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>After trying to make this chocolate sauce at home, you will never go back to store-bought syrup again. No weird preservatives or ingredients like the ones in the store. You will &nbsp;need two ingredients to make this delicious sauce.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Watch this <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/BjIktIpBn4P/?taken-by=cafegourmandnatalija\">quick video</a> to make your mouth water.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe {\"id\":21595,\"template\":\"chic-template-english\",\"updated\":1615140321970} -->\n<!--WPRM Recipe 21595-->\n<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe\">\n\t<h2 class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-name\">Chocolate sauce</h2>\n\t<img class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-image\" src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/05/IMG_9820.Blog_-150x150.png\"/>\t<p class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-summary\">\n\t\tYour sauce will taste even better if you will use heavy cream. Unfortunatly most of the time I use milk, since I'm always trying to lose weight 😉 but it keeps finding me for some reason. \t</p>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-equipment\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-ingredients\">\n\t\t<ul><li>125 ml milk or heavy cream</li><li>150 g dark chocolate (60-70%)</li></ul>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-instructions\">\n\t\t<ol><li>In a small saucepan bring milk (or cream) to boil. Remove from the heat and pour the liquid over the chocolate. Allow it to sit for 1 minute. Whisk to combine.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/05/IMG_9782.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>The sauce will stay loose while its hot. But you can always reheat it. Spoon the chocolate mixture into a heatproof bowl set over a saucepan of simmering water. Heat the sauce for about 3-4 minutes stirring constantly or until it has become liquid again.  <br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/05/IMG_9790.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li></ol>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-notes\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta\">\n\t\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta-course\">Dessert</div>\t</div>\n</div>\n<!--End WPRM Recipe-->\n<!-- /wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe -->",
    "excerpt": null
  },
